# Render (and most PaaS) set NODE_ENV=production, which makes npm default to
# `omit=dev` and skip devDependencies entirely. The build needs them: `tsc`
# itself, and every @types/* package. Without this the deploy fails with ~40
# TS7016/TS2304/TS2591 errors — "Cannot find name 'fetch'", "Cannot find name
# 'console'", "Could not find a declaration file for module 'express'" — none of
# which reproduce locally, because a local install has the dev tree.
#
# `include` takes precedence over `omit`, so this restores devDependencies at
# install time without having to change NODE_ENV (which the app itself reads,
# via src/env.ts) or move build-only packages into `dependencies`.
include=dev
